# Build artifacts. Upstream ships no .gitignore, so a plain `git add -A` after a
# build sweeps 50+ object files into the commit — which is exactly what happened
# on the first attempt here. The engine source is what has to be public, not the
# leftovers of one machine's compiler.
build/
*.o
*.d
*.elf
*.nso
*.npdm
*.nacp
*.lst
*.map
*.ovl
*.nro
